    "text": "Let's denote the amount of money Randy had initially as \\( x \\) dollars.\n\n1. Smith gave Randy $200, so Randy's new amount of money is:\n   \\[\n   x + 200\n   \\]\n\n2. Randy then gave Sally $1,200, so the amount of money Randy has left is:\n   \\[\n   (x + 200) - 1200\n   \\]\n\n3. According to the problem, Randy has $2000 left. Therefore, we can set up the following equation:\n   \\[\n   (x + 200) - 1200 = 2000\n   \\]\n\n4. Simplify the left side of the equation:\n   \\[\n   x + 200 - 1200 = 2000\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   x - 1000 = 2000\n   \\]\n\n5. To find \\( x \\), add 1000 to both sides of the equation:\n   \\[\n   x = 2000 + 1000\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   x = 3000\n   \\]\n\nSo, the amount of money Randy had at first is \\(\\boxed{3000}\\).",
